---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const updated = 'November 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — AniScroll"
  description="How AniScroll handles your library, online dictionary lookups, backups, and website data."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main" class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <div class="legal-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Privacy</span>
        <h1>Privacy, without the fine print.</h1>
        <p>
          AniScroll is designed to keep your library on your device. This page explains what the
          app stores, when it uses the network, and what the website does.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-body">
        <section>
          <h2>Your library stays on your device</h2>
          <p>
            AniScroll does not require an account. Your manga, anime, novels, reading progress,
            settings, and downloaded content are stored locally on your device unless you choose
            to export a backup or use an optional integration.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Online dictionary lookups</h2>
          <p>
            When the online dictionary fallback is enabled, the word you look up is sent to the
            selected provider so a definition can be returned. Japanese lookups use Jisho and
            JMdict data. Chinese, Korean, and other languages use Wiktionary.
          </p>
          <p>
            Only the search term is sent for a dictionary lookup. The fallback can be disabled at
            any time in AniScroll's dictionary settings to keep lookups fully offline.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Sources, extensions, and media</h2>
          <p>
            AniScroll can connect to content sources, extension repositories, video hosts, and
            other network services that you choose to use. Those services operate independently
            and have their own privacy policies. AniScroll does not control how they handle
            requests.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Backups</h2>
          <p>
            Backups are created only when you request them. You can optionally protect a backup
            with a password using AES-256-GCM encryption and PBKDF2 key derivation. If you lose
            the password, AniScroll cannot recover it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>
            The AniScroll website is a static site. It does not set cookies, run advertising, or
            include third-party analytics. The download section may request the latest release
            information from GitHub's public API.
          </p>
          <p>
            The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub, as the hosting provider, may process
            standard request information such as IP addresses for security and operational
            purposes under its own privacy policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Open source and contact</h2>
          <p>
            AniScroll is an independent open-source project. If you have a privacy question or
            want to report a problem, open an issue on
            <a href={site.issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a new
            date. Continued use of AniScroll after an update means the revised policy applies.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
